                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/10660</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sharp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-04T23:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 4, 1918, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 5, 10.16
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5714. War Trade Board [from Stetson]:</p>
                <p>No. 566. Referring Department’s 5937, October 17, your No. 383.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d200-f1"/> We are advised by His Britannic Majesty’s delegate,
                    Paris, that (1) British Government will not make a more definite reply to
                    Spanish note protesting against the black lists than that already made, (2) it
                    is therefore not necessary to ask you to say anything to the Spanish Government
                    at the moment, and (3) that the matter can be dropped unless further action is
                    taken by the Spanish Government. We would appreciate being kept informed when
                    any protest is received by you and, if so, what answer you make. Stetson.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
